  "description_html": "Skeletal diagram of the Cuban pliosaurid <i>Gallardosaurus iturraldei</i>. The known material is shown in white and based on its original description.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Gasparini2009_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Gasparini2009-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Gray represents restored material, mostly modeled after <i>Peloneustes philarchus</i>,<sup id=\"cite_ref-Ketchum2011_2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Ketchum2011-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-Book_3-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Book-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> slightly modified after <i>Pliosaurus kevani</i><sup id=\"cite_ref-Pliosaurus_4-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Pliosaurus-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> to appear more generic. While sometimes considered a close relative of <i>Peloneustes</i>, a more recent analysis failed to recover a stable position for it.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Sachicasaurus_5-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Sachicasaurus-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"References\">References</h4></div>\n<ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-Gasparini2009-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-Gasparini2009_1-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">Gasparini, Zulma (2009). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/pdf/10.1111/j.1475-4983.2009.00871.x\">A new Oxfordian pliosaurid (Plesiosauria, Pliosauridae) in the Caribbean seaway</a>\". <i>Palaeontology</i> <b>52</b> (3): 661–669.</cite></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-Ketchum2011-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-Ketchum2011_2-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">Ketchum, Hilary F.; Benson, Roger J. (2011). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/pdf/10.1111/j.1475-4983.2011.01050.x\">The cranial anatomy and taxonomy of <i>Peloneustes philarchus</i> (Sauropterygia, Pliosauridae) from the Peterborough member (Callovian, Middle Jurassic) of the United Kingdom</a>\". <i>Palaeontology</i> <b>54</b> (3): 639–665.</cite></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-Book-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-Book_3-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite class=\"book\" style=\"font-style:normal\" id=\"Reference-Andrews-1913\">Andrews, Charles William (1913)      <i> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/125534#page/90/mode/2up%7C\">A descriptive catalogue of the marine reptiles of the Oxford clay. Based on the Leeds Collection in the British Museum (Natural History), London</a></i>, 2, British Museum (Natural History). Department of Geology  <small></small></cite></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-Pliosaurus-4\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-Pliosaurus_4-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">Benson, R. B. J.; Evans, M.; Smith, A. S.; Sassoon, J.; Moore-Faye, S.; Ketchum, H. F.; Forrest, R. (2013). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3669260\">A Giant Pliosaurid Skull from the Late Jurassic of England</a>\". <i>PLoS ONE</i> <b>8</b> (5): e65989. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_object_identifier\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Digital object identifier\">DOI</a></span>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0065989\">10.1371/journal.pone.0065989</a>. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PubMed\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:PubMed\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">PMID</span></a></span> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/23741520\">23741520</a>. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PubMed_Central\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:PubMed Central\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">PMC</span></a></span>: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3669260\">3669260</a>.</cite></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-Sachicasaurus-5\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-Sachicasaurus_5-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">Páramo-Fonseca, María Eurídice, Cristian David Benavides-Cabra, and Ingry Esmirna Gutiérrez (2018). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.scielo.org.co/scielo.php?script=sci_arttext&amp;pid=S1794-61902018000400223\">A new large Pliosaurid from the Barremian (Lower Cretaceous) of Sáchica, Boyacá, Colombia</a>\". <i>Earth Sciences Research Journal</i> <b>22</b> (4): 223-238.</cite></span>\n</li>\n</ol>",
